# Synthetic findings and commit metadata; real store, source captures and TUI.
name: Review distinguishes the source of an older verdict from later observations
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_source.py prepare @TMP_TARGET @ART/fixture
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/fixture/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 DECISION SOURCE | older-decision
expect: fixture-a
expect: 111111111111
expect: fixture-b
expect: 222222222222
expect: Reassess this verdict
ask: Does Review retain the older human verdict while naming both recorded revisions and the need for reassessment, with no fix claim or new scan?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 DECISION SOURCE | source-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 DECISION SOURCE | source-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | source-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | source-60x20
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 ZOOM SELECTED FINDING | source-focus
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | source-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: source-40x12-page-1
keys: NPage
live-snap: source-40x12-page-2
keys: NPage
live-snap: source-40x12-page-3
keys: NPage
live-snap: source-40x12-page-4
keys: NPage
live-snap: source-40x12-page-5
ask: At 40x12, can the operator page from the verdict into its source warning without losing the selected finding?
resize: 120x36
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | restored-source
keys: PPage
require-live-snap: 20 recorded: confirmed | source-before-new-decision
submit: decision deferred Synthetic source B deliberately deferred
require-live-snap: 30 No later observation | reassessed-source
expect: recorded: deferred
expect: Synthetic source B deliberately deferred
expect: fixture-b
expect: No later observation
ask: Does the explicit new verdict use source B, retain the earlier decisions and avoid treating absence as a fix?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/fixture/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Synthetic source B deliberately deferred | source-restarted
expect: fixture-b
expect: No later observation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_source.py verify @TMP_TARGET @ART/fixture
ask: Does no-color restart retain the new source-qualified verdict and all prior decisions with unchanged source and zero provider work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
